 "text": "Hey, nice to hear from you. How are you? Sure. In a colour model with more than three primary colours, one colour is made by mixing two others, and its opposite is the other two. Complementary colours look loud against each other. If you add little of the complementary, you can make greys that feel almost black. Yes, and it less likely to look muddy. And the greys are more even across the whole light to dark range. That' a great experiment. Test it on a small piece first.",
